# Transformer development discipline

Adapted for this repository from the cross-platform "LLM Code Transformer Skills Suite"
(transformer-core, verification-suite, continuous-improver — see
`knowledge/sources/llm-transformer-skills-suite.md`). Only the parts that earn their
keep here are kept.

## The invariant that outranks every other

**The transformer must never change what a note says.** A rewrite is either
deterministic-language-only or it is a judgment call handed back to a human. Before
touching `src/lib/standardize/`, `src/lib/vocab/`, `src/lib/audit/`, or
`src/lib/assist/`, read the header comment of `standardize.ts` and the tests in
`meaning.test.ts` and `property.test.ts` — they are the contract.

## Verification loop (non-negotiable, in this order)

1. **Storm first.** For any new vocab entry or rule, write the adversarial case before
   the implementation: casing variants, plurals, sentence boundaries, medical-history
   collisions (the NKA/FMS/Coe-Pak class), idempotency ×3.
2. `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.
3. `npm test` — the full suite, not just the touched files. The property suites in
   `src/lib/standardize/property.test.ts` exist to catch you.
4. `npm run build` before any PR update.
5. Commit per logical change with a message that states the harm the change prevents,
   not just what it does.

## Versioning discipline

- Any change to audit rules, module definitions, or controlled vocabulary bumps
  `RULESET_VERSION` in `src/lib/version.ts`, with a one-line note.
- Any change to an AI system prompt bumps `ASSIST_PROMPT_VERSION` in
  `src/lib/assist/prompts.ts`.
- Frozen historical submissions are immutable. Never write a migration that rewrites
  filed note or audit text.

## AI layer rules

- Every model output passes `verifyMeaning()` before a human sees it. If you add an AI
  capability, decide its verifier mode ("rewrite" or "questions") first and add
  adversarial-model tests in `src/lib/assist/service.test.ts` that prove refusal.
- The PHI gate runs before any provider call. No exceptions, no override paths.
- The model is injected (`GenerateFn`) — tests bind adversaries, never live providers.

## Continuous improvement memory

Durable insights go where the repo already keeps them:

- Research and source digests → `knowledge/sources/` (with the INDEX.md entry).
- Defect post-mortems worth remembering → comments at the fix site plus a pinned
  regression test. This codebase's convention is that the comment tells the story of
  the bug; keep doing that.
- Recurring staff-facing wording decisions → `skill/references/` is DEPRECATED as a
  source of truth; the vocab tables and `/reference` pages are the single truth.

## Tone in user-facing text

Cold logic, zero condescension: state WHAT was found, WHY the line stops, HOW to move.
Never scold, never hype. Encouragement is earned (first-pass clean) and specific.
